Package: vabaxos-accessibility
Architecture: all
Maintainer: VabaxOS <https://github.com/Vabax-dev/VabaxOS>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: espeakup, espeak-ng, orca, triggerhappy, alsa-utils, wireplumber, procps, speech-dispatcher-espeak-ng, speech-dispatcher-audio-plugins, init-system-helpers
Description: VabaxOS accessibility defaults
 Speech from the first second (ADR-0005, ADR-0014): Speakup with
 eSpeak NG reads the text console, and Orca starts in the desktop.
 The boot option vabaxos.voice=off turns both off.
 The GNOME Shell extension button-names@vabaxos.org names the buttons
 that show only an icon, such as Close and Expand on notifications
 (ADR-0022).
 Ctrl+Super+Enter brings the voice back from anywhere, even when the
 desktop is frozen: triggerhappy reads the keys and
 /usr/libexec/vabaxos/voice-rescue starts sound, speech-dispatcher, Orca
 and console speech again, with eSpeak NG.
